Receipt IV — uniform 90-day histories, all eligible exposure rows
Release 1.0.0 | 20 October 2026

RUN

Download Receipt_IV_Uniform90_v1_0_0.zip to ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop.
Extract it, then run:

bash "$HOME/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/Receipt_IV_Uniform90_v1_0_0/RUN_UNIFORM90.command" --project "/Volumes/XT_Pro/lichess_kindness" --workers 10 --memory-gb 11

The launcher checks package hashes and runs the included tests. It reuses a
compatible existing Python environment, or creates a separate environment and
installs requirements.txt. Python 3.10+ is required. On macOS it uses caffeinate.
Do not run other research pipelines concurrently. The runner checks their locks.
Allow at least 100 GiB free on the project drive; temporary disk demand depends
on the newly eligible comparison frame and DuckDB spill.

The primary receipt analysis uses authenticated local caches. The expanded
entry/placebo frame may need previously uncached game metadata. It first reuses
authenticated metadata, including the completed v1.0.3 rebuild, then fetches
only unresolved eligible game IDs with the existing serial downloader. It does
not run Stockfish. To prohibit metadata requests, append --offline. If records
are missing, the runner retains the receipt results and exports a needs report;
rerun without --offline to continue. It never silently drops unresolved games.

Append --preflight-only to authenticate the main existing inputs and stop.
Rerun the same command after interruption or failure. Completed files are
checked and reused; an input or checksum mismatch is an error, not an excuse
to substitute a different sample. Keep the extracted package directory and
project checkpoints while the run is in progress.

WHAT CHANGES

* Keep every eligible competitive receipt exposure; no spacing and no cap of
  one row per recipient. Repeated recipients and shared future choices remain.
* Recipient behavioral counts use [exposure game start - 90 days, game start).
  There is no seven-day gap. The lower endpoint is included; the upper endpoint
  is excluded. History coverage therefore requires 90 days rather than 97.
* Prior playing volume uses game starts in that same 90-day interval, replacing
  the prior 30-day count. This preserves the original factual chronology
  convention. It is NOT a count of completed games: the minimal all-game
  chronology contains start timestamps, not decision/end timestamps. Behavioral
  histories continue to use the inherited decision timestamp and clean counts.
* Seven recent behavioral balance traits also use 90 days. Volume is an eighth
  trait. They are tested jointly under NH+ENV with recipient-history controls
  omitted. A trait controlled for in the primary model is not treated as
  independent evidence of balance.

WHAT IS RETAINED

All-time pooled state-adjusted Score A; donor-own-month held-out-pair-fold state
reference; removal of all focal-pair donor decisions; at least five donor
decisions; expected donor rate and donor size/breadth controls; existing other
controls, fixed effects, ENV definitions, and fixed score scale 0.04979005187533171.
Author accounts __PRIVATE_VALUE_1__ and __PRIVATE_VALUE_2__ remain excluded from exposures, donors,
state references and behavioral histories. Factual all-game chronology remains
unchanged. Existing source files and prior analysis outputs are read only.

The outcome is the first later qualifying competitive chooser decision, in
inherited deterministic order (decision time, archive ordinal, game ID). Its
game must start strictly after the exposure's last-move timestamp, involve a
different opponent and be decided no later than anchor + 90 days. A missing
qualifying later choice is zero, not missing. The inherited complete-followup
cut anchor + 90 days < panel end remains. The prior outcome is reproduced
exactly on all 3,103,280 legacy primary rows before results can proceed.

Uncertainty uses the same shared-account-OR-exposure-date CR0 formula. The
implementation groups complete cluster keys in bounded disk partitions and
retains cross-sample covariance in contrasts. Nonpositive/indefinite covariance
is reported as unsupported, not clipped. Generated scores are treated as fixed.
More rows are not asserted to be the same number of independent observations.

COMPARISONS AND DIAGNOSTICS

The receipt report estimates six explicitly named models:
1. Legacy spaced rows with their legacy features; coefficients AND standard
   errors must reproduce the verified R12 total-five reference.
2. Exactly the same rows with immediate 90-day histories and 90-day volume.
3. Uniform90 on the legacy spacing rule, with the seven earlier days admitted.
4. Uniform90 without spacing, restricted to the legacy calendar eligibility.
5. Uniform90 without spacing over the complete newly eligible calendar.
6. Model 5's balance specification with recipient histories omitted as controls.

The legacy spacing algorithm is used only for comparisons. It applies the
strict start > previous accepted anchor + 90d rule after donor support but
before observation-window cuts, as in the accepted prior run.

Contrasts separately estimate the history change on identical rows, spacing
change at a fixed calendar range, and calendar gain. sample_counts.csv reports
actual row and recipient counts; the early gain is NOT assumed to be exactly
seven rows per recipient. It depends on eligible observed exposure events.

overlap_audit.json reports repeated recipients, overlapping followup windows,
shared future choices, and later retained exposures before the assigned
outcome. These are exposure-weighted estimates. Spacing never established that
no unsupported or otherwise unretained receipt occurred between anchors.

Entry and ordinary placebo are rebuilt on the same full Phase100 additional-
game hash frame, preserving deterministic focal orientation, prior-pilot
exclusion, author rules, first observed pair and predecessor eligibility.
The receipt cooldown is removed, coverage becomes 90 days, and support remains
all-time-five. Old selected comparison rows are not used as the new frame.
Newly eligible rows use cached local chronology scans where possible; missing
chronology is recomputed from local files with a bounded merge. Metadata is
resolved before estimating. Both frames receive the same new histories and
volume. Entry labels refer to the unspaced supported receipt cohort. The
ordinary placebo retains its original status and followup criteria. Both
receive fresh balance estimates; receipt-minus-ordinary covariance is retained.
The original placebo equivalence margin is converted to the same fixed score
scale. Existing diagnostic numbers are never relabeled as new results.

OUTPUTS AND RESUMPTION

New local research files:
derived/replication/receipt_iv_uniform90_v100_PRIVATE/<configuration prefix>/

Desktop reports:
UNIFORM90_IV_<configuration prefix>_025.zip — selection and sample counts
UNIFORM90_IV_<configuration prefix>_050.zip — rebuilt receipt features
UNIFORM90_IV_<configuration prefix>_075.zip — receipt estimates and contrasts
UNIFORM90_IV_<configuration prefix>_100.zip — expanded diagnostics complete

Each report has a .sha256 sidecar. Reports contain aggregate results and logs;
observation-level data and influences stay in PRIVATE. A failed later stage
exports an updated status at the last milestone. Inspect STATUS.json: a 075
file is not a completed entry/placebo run. Return the 100 ZIP and its sidecar
for review; if stopped, return the latest report ZIP instead.

The 25/50/75/100 labels are stage milestones, not percentages of elapsed time.
The code logs heartbeats and measured task/partition ETAs where available.
Total runtime for this new expanded frame has not been benchmarked. At most
two large local jobs run together; statistical models and metadata requests
run serially. --workers 10 is a ceiling, not a promise of ten concurrent jobs.
The allocation policy targets the 11 GiB budget; it is not an OS-level RSS cap.

VALIDATION AND LIMITS

Twelve synthetic/integration tests cover the history and followup boundaries,
author exclusion, repeated/shared outcomes, all-game volume versus a brute
force oracle, signature checking, resumed outputs, the separate calendar and
spacing gains, expanded candidate selection, chronology scan/merge, comparison
labels and ordinary selection, exact legacy model transforms and estimates,
and CR0 versus a direct pairwise OR calculation including duplicated rows.
All passed in the build environment. TEST_RESULTS.txt records the checks.

The 798 vendored source/evidence files are byte identical to the retrieved
AllTime_Entry_Placebo_v1_0_5 package. All new behavior lives in the top-level
uniform_*.py files and run_uniform90.py. SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json records hashes.
The original package's reviewed R12/R9/cache contracts remain enforced.

The actual external-drive research data are not present in the build
environment. Full-data execution, actual added-row counts, runtime, and new
estimates await your Mac run. The legacy reproduction gate and exact outcome
bridge protect the full-data handoff; they are not replaced by synthetic tests.
